lhaut_%28weic2312a%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Astronomers used the James Webb Space Telescope to image the warm dust around a nearby young star, Fomalhaut, to study the first asteroid belt ever seen outside the Solar System in infrared light.[26]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWebb_inspects_dusty_debris_disc_around_Fomalhaut_(weic2312a).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/A_glowing_jet_from_a_young_star.tif/lossy-page1-500px-A_glowing_jet_from_a_young_star.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/A_glowing_jet_from_a_young_star.tif/lossy-page1-500px-A_glowing_jet_from_a_young_star.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"HH 151 is a bright jet of glowing material trailed by an intricate, orange-hued plume of gas and dust.[29] ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_glowing_jet_from_a_young_star.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2f/Smooth_chondriteIDP.jpg/500px-Smooth_chondriteIDP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2f/Smooth_chondriteIDP.jpg/500px-Smooth_chondriteIDP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Smooth chondrite interplanetary dust particle.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmooth_chondriteIDP.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}